course: dictionary
lesson: 1645
title: Chilly: cold, and cold to people
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Chilly means rather cold, cold enough to make you uncomfortable. «Meanwhile the others warm their chilly toes by the fire» tells you the toes were cold, and the fire is there to warm them up.
explain: Chilly can also describe a person or a welcome. It means unfriendly, not warm. If someone gives you a chilly look, they are not being kind or friendly, even though the air around them may not be cold at all.
explain: Look at the words near chilly to choose the right meaning. A chilly morning, a chilly wind, and feel chilly are about temperature. A chilly welcome and a chilly reply are about feelings between people.
fact: Chilly means rather cold, cold enough to be uncomfortable.
fact: A chilly person or welcome is unfriendly and not warm.
fact: «Meanwhile the others warm their chilly toes by the fire» means the toes are cold.
fact: «Being chilly on your own, with nobody's germs about, does not give you a cold» shows that feeling cold does not cause a cold.
fact: Colds are caused by viruses, which you catch from other people.
exercise: «Meanwhile the others warm their chilly toes by the fire.» What does chilly mean here? | Dark and quiet | Very hot and sweaty | Very rude and angry | *Rather cold, uncomfortable
exercise: «Colds are caused by viruses caught from other people; being chilly with wet hair doesn't create a virus.» What causes a cold, according to this? | Being chilly on your own | *Viruses caught from other people | Shutting the windows | Being chilly with wet hair
exercise: «She gave me a chilly look and did not say hello.» What does chilly suggest here? | Sleepy and tired | *Unfriendly, not warm | Hungry for lunch | Friendly and warm
test: Put on a jumper, it is chilly outside this morning. What does chilly mean? | *Rather cold | Very hot | Very rude | Dark
test: The new girl got a chilly welcome from the class, with no smiles at all. What does a chilly welcome mean? | Warm and loving | *Unfriendly and not warm | A welcome with snow | Very noisy and loud
exam: Which phrase uses chilly to mean unfriendly, not cold? | a chilly morning | a chilly wind | *a chilly reply | chilly toes
